---
import Section from './Section.astro';
// A faithfully rendered coach exchange. Voice + rules per docs/COACH_PROMPT.md;
// the tool call, inline [note_id] citations, the personal-finding distinction,
// and "numbers only from tool results" are the coach loop from INTELLIGENCE.md §4.
// recovery_readiness is a real corpus note id (grade: Probable).
---

<Section id="coach" tone="sunk" labelledby="coach-h">
  <h2 id="coach-h" class="rise mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,3rem)]">
    Ask it anything. It looks up your real numbers before it answers.
  </h2>
  <p class="lede rise mt-6 max-w-2xl">
    An unchecked coach can say whatever sounds good. Ours pulls your actual data, backs every claim
    with a research note or your own history, and stays as sure as the evidence lets it be — no more.
  </p>

  <figure
    class="surface surface-lift rise mt-10 max-w-3xl p-6 sm:p-8"
    aria-label="Rendered example: a coach exchange about a weekly HRV dip"
  >
    <figcaption class="mb-6 flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
      <span class="mono text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-ink-faint">
        Conversation &middot; example
      </span>
      <span class="chip chip-accent chip-dot">grounded coach</span>
    </figcaption>

    <div class="turn turn-user">
      <span class="turn-who">You asked</span>
      <p class="turn-body">&ldquo;Why is my HRV down this week?&rdquo;</p>
    </div>

    <!-- the visible mechanism -->
    <div class="toolcall mt-6" role="group" aria-label="The lookup the coach ran">
      <span class="toolcall-tag">
        <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span> looked up your data &middot; query_metric
      </span>
      <div>
        <span class="k">{'{'} metric:</span> <span class="v">"hrv_sleep_avg"</span><span class="k"
          >, window:</span
        > <span class="v">"7d"</span><span class="k">, stat:</span> <span class="v">"series"</span>
        <span class="k">{'}'}</span>
        <span class="ret"
          >&larr; returns: 7 nights &middot; avg <span class="v">39&nbsp;ms</span> &middot; your usual
          <span class="v">46&nbsp;&plusmn;&nbsp;6&nbsp;ms</span></span
        >
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="turn turn-coach mt-6">
      <span class="turn-who">Coach</span>
      <div class="turn-body">
        <p>
          Your overnight heart-rate steadiness has run about <span class="mono">39</span> this week
          against your usual <span class="mono">46&nbsp;&plusmn;&nbsp;6</span> &mdash; a real dip, not
          just night-to-night noise <span class="cite">[recovery_readiness]</span>. It’s a recovery
          signal, but a jumpy one, so I’m reading the whole week, not any single morning.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Before you blame lost fitness, check your log: on the three nights you noted a late drink,
          it dropped the next morning
          <span class="cite cite-personal">[personal finding: late alcohol &rarr; lower HRV]</span>
          &mdash; that’s <em>your</em> pattern, not a population average pinned onto you.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Smallest lever this week: two alcohol-free nights, then we re-read the trend. I won’t call
          seven confounded days a recovery loss.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <hr class="hairline my-6" />

    <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <p class="mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
        <span class="text-accent-soft">[recovery_readiness]</span> is a real research note in the
        library — you can open it and read the evidence yourself. The
        <span class="text-warn">amber tag</span> marks a pattern from your own data, never dressed up
        as research.
      </p>
      <p class="mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
        Every number here came from the <span class="text-ink">query_metric</span> lookup above. The
        coach never guesses your numbers — if a lookup didn’t return it, it doesn’t have it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </figure>
</Section>
